% Documentation generated by roxygen2.
% Historical documentation source: R/select_genotypes.R
\name{select.genotypes}
\alias{select.genotypes}
\title{Selects specific allele combinations from populations}
\usage{
select.genotypes(newPop, oldPop, criteria)
}
\arguments{
\item{newPop}{a character string specifying the name of the new population which is created from the selected genotype(s).}

\item{oldPop}{a character string specifying the name of the population that selection is applied to.}

\item{criteria}{a data.frame containing the locinames and the selection criteria for selection. Every row is one criterion.
Data.frame must contain three columns: locusname, allele 1, allele 2.}
}
\value{
On successful completion, returns the invisible implementation-level \code{list} produced by the final temporary-population removal. If the source population is empty, \code{NULL} is returned invisibly. The meaningful result is the side effect of constructing \code{newPop} according to the requested allele criteria.
}
\description{
This function is used to select individuals from a population that fulfill certain selection criteria.
}
\details{
Individuals are selected based on their genotypes at the loci listed in
`criteria`. Genotype matching is performed using internally created effects.

If multiple rows are provided for the same `locus`, an individual matches
that locus if it satisfies **any** of the rows for that locus (OR within
locus). Individuals must satisfy the requirements for **all** loci present
in `criteria` (AND across loci).

Selected individuals are removed from `oldPop` and added to `newPop`.
}
\examples{
data("v-tropmaize-vcf", package = "SelectionTools")
marker.frame <- st.STvcf.to.dataframe(v.tropmaize.vcf)[1:12, c(1:6, 7:14)]
vcf <- st.dataframe.to.STvcf(marker.frame)
st.load.vcf.data(vcf, data.set = "maize.example")
reset.all()
st.set.sim.gp(data.set = "maize.example")
st.set.sim.mp(data.set = "maize.example")
st.set.sim.pp("Maize", data.set = "maize.example")
loci <- vcf$ID
observed <- evaluate.genotype("Maize", loci[1], bg = 1)
criteria <- data.frame(locus = loci[1],
                        allele1 = as.integer(observed[[1]][1]),
                        allele2 = as.integer(observed[[2]][1]))
select.genotypes("Selected", "Maize", criteria)
evaluate.genotype("Selected", loci[1])
}
